  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Gauge",
    "overview": "Headroom is a gauge that lives inside someone else's dashboard. It has no world of its own: every colour is a named colour of the running Herdr theme, read from `theme()` at render, and the type is Herdr's UI font (Geist) with its terminal font (JetBrains Mono) for codes and addresses. What it owns is a structure, the pair of bars, and a temperament: Claude-like restraint, few symbols, states written as words, shapes drawn rather than typed as terminal glyphs.\n\nThe surface is glanced at between other work, in the left sidebar beside Herdr's Spaces and Agents mods. It is dense and calm. Nothing carries colour until something is wrong: at rest every fill and number is `muted`, and the theme's `working` and `blocked` appear only when a window passes 75 % and 90 %. The bar always keeps its full width; the numbers sit in one quiet 11 px line beneath it and never take the bar's room.\n\nThe values in the frontmatter are the graphite theme (Herdr's default dark). They are a reference, not constants: the code names the role (`t.chrome`, `t.muted`) and paper, ink, moss and atom-one-dark supply their own values for the same names.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Thickness names the window: a full 6 px bar for a weekly window, a 3 px bar for the 5-hour one, 4 px apart.",
      "Colour only for trouble; a level is always paired with its number or the words \"At limit\".",
      "A 2 px pace tick with a ground-coloured halo says whether an account is burning faster than its window.",
      "Herdr's own provider marks, spinner, scrollbar, confirm dialog and toasts; no brand, logo or palette of the mod's own.",
      "Native motion only: fills and ticks slide with `.transition`, waits spin with `.spin(900)`."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colour Is Trouble Rule",
        "body": "At rest, everything is `muted` or `foreground`. `working` and `blocked` appear only when a window is high, critical or at its limit, and `accent` only on what can be clicked to fix something.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never By Colour Alone Rule",
        "body": "A level is always beside its number; at 100 % the number becomes the words \"At limit\". Nothing is told by hue only.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Theme Owns The Values Rule",
        "body": "Never write a hex value in the mod. Name the theme role; derive anything else (track, level numbers, badge tint) from theme roles with `mix()` and `alpha()`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Words Not Glyphs Rule",
        "body": "States are written: \"At limit\", \"Sign in again\", \"not started\", \"12m old · network\". No warning triangles, no terminal block characters. The only typed symbol is the \"·\" separator in `dim`, and the compact \"!\" badge copied from Herdr.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Number Rule",
        "body": "Percentages and countdowns are 11 px and `muted` under the bar; they never get a column of their own beside it. Format: \"41% · 4d 6h\"; alone on a row, \"23% · resets in 5d 2h\".",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Card Rule",
        "body": "No borders, pills or containers around an account. The pair of bars and the 9 px gap are the grouping.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** name theme roles (`t.chrome`, `t.muted`) and derive the rest with `mix()` and `alpha()`; the mod follows every Herdr theme, light and dark.",
      "**Do** keep the weekly bar full (6 px) and the 5-hour bar thin (3 px), 4 px apart, at the full width, in every form.",
      "**Do** put the percentage and reset under the bar in 11 px `muted`, with the level colour only on the percentage.",
      "**Do** mix level colours 22 % toward `foreground` for text, so every readable number holds 4.5:1 on graphite and paper.",
      "**Do** draw only the windows a plan reports; a weekly-only account has one bar.",
      "**Do** reuse Herdr's assets: provider marks (`icons/claude.svg`, `icons/codex.svg`), spinner, plus and chevron icons, scrollbar, confirm dialog, toasts.",
      "**Do** move a bar to a new reading with `.transition`; nothing pulses or redraws on a timer for motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** write a hex value in the mod or give it a logo, brand colour or palette of its own.",
      "**Don't** tell a level by colour alone, or colour anything at rest.",
      "**Don't** give the numbers a column beside the bar, or shorten the bar to fit them.",
      "**Don't** wrap accounts in cards, borders or pills, or sort them by usage.",
      "**Don't** use terminal glyphs, block characters or warning symbols; write the state as words.",
      "**Don't** use `dim` for anything a person must read beyond where Herdr's own mods use it.",
      "**Don't** add a collapse control to the list, or a grouping setting."
    ]
  }
}
